<title>USA: Nebraska $50 mln agency bonds repriced, yields cut.</title>
<headline>Nebraska $50 mln agency bonds repriced, yields cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Wednesday it repriced Nebraska Investment Finance Authority's $50 million bond deal, lowering yields five basis points in the serial maturities.</p>
<p>Nebraska Investment Finance Authority</p>
<p>RE: $50,000,000*</p>
<p>Single Family Housing Revenue Bonds</p>
<p>1997 Series B</p>
<p>Verbal award.</p>
<p>Note repricing on the serials.</p>
<p>SUBJECT TO ALTERNATIVE MINIMUM TAX</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: NAF		 S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>    DATED: 07/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 09/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 09/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
